Subject: Generate pointer-valued once initialization at every GLib target
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Fil-C target integration

GType is a pointer under Fil-C. Below --target-glib=2.80 valac stored
type IDs and regex literals in gsize once variables and returned them as
GType, which clang rejects (-Wint-conversion) and which would drop the
pointer's capability anyway. Always use the GLib 2.80 path: GType storage
with g_once_init_enter_pointer/g_once_init_leave_pointer. The target GLib
is 2.80.4.

The shipped C for the two codegen files is patched to match, so the build
valac needs no bootstrap valac. ports/build-tools.nix applies this to the
valac whose target is Fil-C; the Fil-C vala regenerates all its C with it.

